<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2017/DarlaR3.jpg" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Darla R (plein air and studio). 9x12, oil on linen panel. 2016/17</p>
<div class="" data-block="true" data-editor="ea7cf" data-offset-key="2q9o0-0-0">
<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="2q9o0-0-0">&nbsp;</div>
</div>
<div class="" data-block="true" data-editor="ea7cf" data-offset-key="bk33i-0-0">
<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="bk33i-0-0"><span data-offset-key="bk33i-0-0"><span data-text="true">Darla R is a plein air work, done on location at the Fisherman's Terminal in Seattle. I always liked the </span></span><a title="view the original painting" href="/blog/darla-r-plein-air-painting-of-a-fishing-boat" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-offset-key="bk33i-1-0"><span data-text="true">original piece</span></span></a><span data-offset-key="bk33i-2-0"><span data-text="true">, but felt that it lacked enough light&nbsp;to make it marketable.</span></span></div>
<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="bk33i-0-0">&nbsp;</div>
<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="bk33i-0-0">It turns out that it was an easy problem to fix. Adding light is easy if your subject is back-lit.</div>
<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="bk33i-0-0">&nbsp;</div>
<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="bk33i-0-0">I repainted the entire background to make it lighter and made some of the boat darker. I also reworked some of the edges on the top of the boat. Taken together these make the light look stronger and provide a gradation in value from the top of the painting to the bottom.</div>
<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="bk33i-0-0">&nbsp;</div>
<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="bk33i-0-0">Where I had to be most careful was in selecting the right temperature for the light. It needed to look warm against the cool grays. And it also needed to be a gray, because I found by trial and error that this worked better if the effect was subtle.</div>
<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="bk33i-0-0">&nbsp;</div>
